      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-10-14_WidnesExaminer_art0001" n="art0001">
        <p>COUNTY PALATINE OF CHESTER. IVOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN, that the neat 11 GENERAL QUARTER SESSIONS of the Peace • for the COUNTY PALATINE OF CHESTER will be holden at the COURT-HOUSE, KNUTSFORD, in and for the said County, on MONDAY, the 15th day of OCTOBER, 1911, at Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon, when the Grand r'nry still de empennelled. The hearing of all Appeals arming within the Petty Seseional Divi,ions of Altrincham, Bucklow, Dukin- field, rit iddlew ioh, Sandbach, Congleton, Northavich, Preatbmy and Stockport, forming the Knotsford District, and the trials of all prisoners committed from such Divisions, viii take place at s,rch sessions. The Grand and Petty Julies for the Enutsford District must be in attendance at the COURT HOUSE, KNUTSFORD, at the opening of the Court on MONDAY, the 16th day of OCTOBER NEXT, at Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon. THE COURT will be Adjourned to the CASTLE OF CHESTER on WEDNESDAY, the 19th day of OCTOBER, 1911, at Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon, when another Grand Jury w ill he empannelled. The hearing of all Appeals arising within the Petty Sessional Divisions or Brenton, Chester Castle, Dares- bury, Eddisbury, Nantwich, Runcorn, Wiasford and Wirral, forming the Chester District, and the trials of all prisoners committed from the last-mentioned Divisions will take place at such Adjourned Sessions. The Grand and Petty Juries for the Chester District must be in attendance at the CASTLE OF CHESTER, st the opening of the Court on WEDNESDAY, the 18th day of October, 1911. at Eteven O'clock in the Forenoon.</p>
        <p>REGINALD POTTS, Clerk of the Peace for the County Cheiter,3rd October, 1911. Palatine of Cheater.</p>
