        <p>to be national property. They also held that tte me of national property for private purposes has inequitable, unjust and criminal. (Applause). The PRESIDENT said a certain minority of the Liberal party was not yet convinced of the expediency or justice of Welsh disestablishenent and she suggested it would be a great advantage if speakers from Wales, who had an intimate knowledge of the feelings of their own countrymen, could addrets meetings of the various associations in the larger towns.</p>
        <p>Mrs. dnsies Buss (North Lenart&amp;le) said the reason why the Church in Wales was the Church of a minority was thst it had failed to study the character and thought of the Welsh people. It was a failing on the pert of English people, wherever they went, that they would not take the trouble to study characters. If they tried to treat the Welsh as English, they could not get the best out of the nation. If the I iberal party stood for anything it stood for justice, and it was unjust that a tiny minority should rule end have all those tremendous endowments. The greatest and most beautiful of all arguments in favour of Disestablishment was that if the Church of Wales—and she believed the Church of Eogland, too were disestabliaed, it would increase its spirituality. In the words of the Bishop of Hereford, 'the spiritual inlinence and poorer of our Anglican Communion will increase as never before." No Establishment should exist against the sill of the people. The true establishment could only be in the bealts of the people. jApplause). The resolution was then carried unanimously in the following terms :—'` That this Council, recognizing the overwhelming demand of the Welsh nation for religious equality during the past forty years, heartily approves of the policy of the Governmeot to secure the Disestab- lishruent and Disendowment of the English Church in Waits, and welcomrs the pledge of the Government to introduce a measure to this effect next session, no that the Bill may become law during the present Parliatimnt."</p>
