        <p>By that methoo ha thought he sht old Ia nble to dispose quite satisfactorily of the suggestion that be wag a capitalist or an it mployer's man. Mtn he was .ut, hie father gave up his ordinary business and w. nt in tot the Ear, but unfotturately be died soon afterwards, at, the financial prosperity of their family vias not net great. hull U wss considered that no sactifice wi.s to great to give his brother (Mr. F. E. Sn ith) a good education. That sacrifice was made, and their fainil3 woe very proud they made it. (Applause.) When Et (tte speat er) left school he was scarcely 16 years et age and he had to soft berth to go to, so he net to ansnering advertisements, and at last get a job. It can not very profitable, but lie did his best and pushed along. Then he got something better and pushed along at that, until big family began to thank that perhaps.he.a as</p>
