      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-10-14_WidnesExaminer_art0033" n="art0033">
        <head>FEARFUL BOUTS OF COUGHING</head>
        <p>FEARFUL BOUTS OF COUGHING</p>
        <p>How Peps Cured a Husband's and Wife's</p>
        <p>Chest Troublcs.</p>
        <p>How the wonderful Pep breatheable tablets are to be relied upon to give permanent relief in the most troublesome chest cases is shown by the experience of Mr. Samuel Holley, aged 73, of 3, Alington Tetraae, Durngate-street, Dorchester. Mr. Holley writes : " After being kept indoors for sometime through an accident, I got cold when I went out again. My throat was very irritable, and when I coughed to get relief I hlegm came up in large quantities. For about three months I took little notice of this new com- plaint, but it then got so troublesome that I had some medicine from my doctor. Bottle after bottle I took without getting a bit better. I then had more liquid medicine from the chemist, with still the same dis- heartening result. Often after a bout of coughing I felt awfully sick, yet I could never get the phlegm away. "Soon after I started with Peps, however, the tickling in my throat stopped troubling me so much, and as a result I didn't cough as often. I found Pips specially soothing at night, when, ass rule, I had my worst bouts. By sticking regularly to Peps I got all the phlegm away and my throat got quite strong, con- sidering my (Id age, and stopped troubling me. "Later on my wife and I got bronchitis and we mmediately struttd taking Peps with the happiest results, for before the complaint got a thorough hold on ns Pepe strengthened our throats and chests and enabled as to throw off the bronchial'. We always keep a box of Pepe in reserve, and lakes few tablets whenever we feel a cold cominicon. Peps always To good, and are a priceless boon.' Of all chemists at Is. I d.or 2s. 9d. a box. Avoid worthies, imitations. Ste "Peps," the registered rade mark, on each box before buying.</p>
      </div>
