        <p>VALUABLE FREEHOLD AND LEASEHOLD PktOPERTY AT PADOATE, ORAPPENHALL AND WARRINOTON. TO BE SOLD BY AUCTION by MR. FRANK HICKMAN, at the BLUE BELL INN, WARRING- TON ON WEDN ESDAY, t he 18th day of OCTOBER 1911 at b o'clock in the afternoon (subject to the Public Sale Conditions of the incorporated Law Society of Liver- pool, and special condit,ins to be then produced), ,LOT 1. ALL. THOSE TWO FREEHOLD MESSUAGES OR DWELLING-HOUSES, Noe: N, and 30, Wilderspool Causeway, at the junction or Cheater-road and Wilderspool-tuad, Warrington. Ocoee annual rentals, £27 Si. This property is situated in close proximity to the Wilderspool Crossings. LOT 2.—ALL THAT FREEHOLD MESSUAOB or DWELLING-HOUSE No 1 Chester rd (formerly called• River rd.), Warrington. Gross annual rental £2l. The property LI at present in the occupation of Mr. J. IT E. Wood. 3.—ALL THAT FREEHOLD MESSUAGE DWELLINOHOUHE situate and being in Victoria rd, Grappenhall, near Wsrrington, known as .` Nesacliffe.' The 'louse is substantially built of brick, stands well up and back from the road, and has the following accommodation, viz. : Three reception rooms, live bed- rooms, w.c, kitchen, scullery, and bathroom with hot and cold water supply. The site comprises about 1000 yards. The house is well planned, and the rrronis are lofty and of good size. The street has lately been brought fully up-to-date and taken over by the local authority, and the apportioned cost falling on this property (over £5O) will be cleared by the Vendor. The house is very near to the London and North-Western Railway Station, and ate) to the tram terminus and affords an excellent opportunity either for occupation or investment.</p>
        <p>• LOT 4.—ALL THAT LEASEHOLD SEMI- DETACHED VILLA situate in Pedgate lane, Warring- ton, and known as "Springfield." The house is occupied by Mr. J. C. Harnngton. Gross annual rental, £26. The tenure is leasehold for a term of 999 years from 25th March, 1899, and is subject to an annual ground rent of £2 tea. LOT S.—ALL THOSE TWO LEASEHOLD SEMI- DETACHED VILLAS situate in-Orford Green (oppo- site Orford Church), Warrington, together with the large gardens thereto. The houses are occupied by Messrs. Brown and Schneider. Gross annual rentals £44 4e. The site of the villas and gardens contains 814 square yards or thereabouts. The tenure is lease- hold tor a term of 999 years computed from 20th May, 1908, and is subject to an annual ground rent of £7 15s. Lla 6. ALL THOSE SIX FREEHOLD ! EIESSUAGES or DWELLING-HOUSES situate and ' being Noe. 1 to 11 (odd numbers Inclusive), James st.; off Buttermarket at, Warrington. Gross annual rentals, £45 108. LOT 7.—ALL THAT LEASEHOLD MESSUAGE or DWELLING-HOUSE situate and being No. 147, Knutaford rd., %Varringtou. Gross annual rental, £l9 10e. The tenure is leasehold for a term of 999 years, computed from the Ist November, 1869, and is subject to the payment of an annual ground rent of £1 13s. 4d. The house contains drawing-coons, sitting- room, kitchen, wash-house, and pantry on the ground floor, two bedrooms on the first floor, and two bed- rooms on the second floor. One of the bedroome is fitted with a bath (hot and cold water) and lavatory. The house is in an excellent state of repair, and the inside decorations are unique, the owner being the tenant of the property. For further particulars as to Lot I application may be madeto Mr. iticherd Urry. bolicitor, Shrewsbury, and es to Lot 5 to Mr. James Bsll, Corporation at. CnamBra, 4Varrington, and as ta all the Lots to the Auctioneer at kin oiler, Lyme St. MR. F. R. ROBERTS, Solicitor. 9, Egypt at, Warrington.</p>
