      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-10-14_WidnesExaminer_art0105" n="art0105">
        <head>PICTURES OF THE WEEK.</head>
        <p>PICTURES OF THE WEEK.</p>
        <p>GUARD OF THE GOVERNOR-GENERAL IN TRIPOLI. Our picture shcws the Turkish Guard outside the Governor-General's Konak in fripoli, which has been partly destroyed by the Italian gun-fire, but is now occupied by Italians. Warships continue to shell Tripoli, to prevent attack by Turkish horsemen, who have fled into the interior and menace the entrance to the town. It is reported that Europeans have already been allowed to enter the town, and that the manager and employees of the Bank of Rome have resumed their duties.</p>
